1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:02,752
<i>You see, Caloy,</i>

2
00:00:04,004 --> 00:00:06,256
<i>Mama wants a complete family.</i>

3
00:00:07,382 --> 00:00:09,467
<i>And I'll give her that.</i>

4
00:00:11,344 --> 00:00:12,721
<i>She wants</i>

5
00:00:13,972 --> 00:00:15,640
<i>to take Papa back.</i>

6
00:00:16,433 --> 00:00:17,976
<i>Is that what you want too?</i>

7
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:20,937
<i>For your father to come back to you?</i>

8
00:00:25,483 --> 00:00:26,901
<i>Dad came to visit me.</i>

9
00:00:29,195 --> 00:00:30,780
<i>He apologized to me.</i>

10
00:00:33,241 --> 00:00:36,619
<i>It turns out he was in jail all this time.</i>

11
00:00:37,245 --> 00:00:39,122
<i>So he was released from jail?</i>

12
00:00:39,205 --> 00:00:41,249
<i>He broke out</i>

13
00:00:41,332 --> 00:00:42,834
<i>with Caloy.</i>

14
00:00:44,461 --> 00:00:45,670
<i>What?!</i>

15
00:00:45,754 --> 00:00:47,213
<i>Dude, I'm sorry.</i>

16
00:00:47,297 --> 00:00:50,091
<i>Why are you only</i>
<i>telling me this now, Jordan?!</i>

17
00:00:50,175 --> 00:00:51,342
<i>Why?!</i>

18
00:00:51,426 --> 00:00:54,971
<i>Because I wanted Caloy</i>
<i>to be back in jail before I told you.</i>

19
00:00:55,055 --> 00:00:57,974
<i>But you didn't catch him,</i>
<i>and you almost died again.</i>

20
00:00:58,058 --> 00:00:59,517
<i>But I didn't die.</i>

21
00:01:00,935 --> 00:01:02,103
<i>Because of him.</i>

22
00:01:02,187 --> 00:01:04,981
<i>Even though your dad saved you,</i>

23
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:07,442
<i>you need to report him to the police.</i>

24
00:01:08,443 --> 00:01:10,195
<i>Even if he's sorry for what he did,</i>

25
00:01:11,863 --> 00:01:13,490
<i>he's still a criminal.</i>

26
00:01:13,573 --> 00:01:15,867
<i>When I saw how you and your father</i>
<i>patched things up,</i>

27
00:01:16,868 --> 00:01:18,203
<i>and how you were happy together,</i>

28
00:01:18,953 --> 00:01:19,913
<i>I thought to myself,</i>

29
00:01:20,955 --> 00:01:25,376
<i>what if my father and I</i>
<i>also patched things up?</i>

30
00:01:31,299 --> 00:01:34,844
<i>I just want to give him a chance</i>
<i>at least to start over.</i>

31
00:01:40,016 --> 00:01:41,476
<i>Ma…</i>

32
00:01:42,977 --> 00:01:46,064
<i>Didn't I tell you to behave here?</i>

33
00:01:46,689 --> 00:01:48,399
<i>Endure it a little longer.</i>

34
00:01:48,483 --> 00:01:50,735
<i>I'll get you out of here soon, okay?</i>

35
00:01:51,319 --> 00:01:53,905
<i>We should be together, not them.</i>

36
00:01:53,988 --> 00:01:56,658
<i>They're painting us as the bad guys?</i>

37
00:01:56,741 --> 00:02:00,745
<i>Since when did it become</i>
<i>acceptable to be a mistress?</i>

38
00:02:08,128 --> 00:02:12,048
He wants to give him a chance
to start a new life?

39
00:02:12,132 --> 00:02:17,011
So he's seriously going to hide
his fugitive father and protect him?

40
00:02:17,095 --> 00:02:21,307
I don't know what's going on
in Jordan's mind, Auntie.

41
00:02:21,391 --> 00:02:25,311
Doesn't he know that he could face charges
because of his father?

42
00:02:25,395 --> 00:02:30,358
I also don't believe that Dino
will help him in finding Caloy.

43
00:02:31,985 --> 00:02:35,280
I don't know, Auntie.
It's giving me a headache.

44
00:02:35,363 --> 00:02:37,949
I'm telling you, you'd better
talk to that friend of yours.

45
00:02:38,032 --> 00:02:42,287
Convince him to surrender his father
to the authorities.

46
00:02:42,370 --> 00:02:43,246
That's the thing.

47
00:02:43,329 --> 00:02:46,291
I've been trying to call him,
but he's not picking up.

48
00:02:47,041 --> 00:02:48,126
[DOORBELL RINGS]

49
00:02:48,209 --> 00:02:49,919
- Oh.
- [OLIVER] I'll get it.

50
00:02:50,003 --> 00:02:52,088
- [BUSY TONE]
- See?

51
00:02:55,049 --> 00:02:57,176
- Who is it?
- It's Bea.

52
00:02:58,595 --> 00:02:59,554
Huh?

53
00:02:59,637 --> 00:03:05,476
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

54
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:12,442
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

55
00:04:10,541 --> 00:04:13,378
[CUTLERY CLINKING]

56
00:04:13,461 --> 00:04:14,587
Thank you.

57
00:04:26,391 --> 00:04:28,935
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

58
00:04:29,018 --> 00:04:30,979
[CLEARS THROAT] Um…

59
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:35,525
How's your job application going?

60
00:04:37,568 --> 00:04:38,653
Um…

61
00:04:40,238 --> 00:04:41,364
It's all good, Pa.

62
00:04:42,115 --> 00:04:43,283
Um…

63
00:04:43,366 --> 00:04:48,204
I'll try to contact my former boss
at the phone repair shop.

64
00:04:48,288 --> 00:04:50,957
But that's only temporary

65
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:55,503
while waiting for a call from
the companies I've applied to.

66
00:04:55,586 --> 00:04:57,547
And while waiting,

67
00:04:58,589 --> 00:05:02,218
I can help with the household chores.

68
00:05:02,302 --> 00:05:04,929
I'll help with stuff like

69
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:07,724
picking up Oliver from school.

70
00:05:07,807 --> 00:05:09,392
Don't bother.

71
00:05:10,059 --> 00:05:11,227
We can manage.

72
00:05:11,936 --> 00:05:14,480
Just focus on finding a job.

73
00:05:16,232 --> 00:05:17,150
Oh.

74
00:05:17,233 --> 00:05:20,445
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

75
00:05:20,528 --> 00:05:22,739
Have some more, Oliver. Here.

76
00:05:22,822 --> 00:05:25,616
He can't. We're monitoring Oliver's diet.

77
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:26,868
He has diabetes.

78
00:05:26,951 --> 00:05:27,952
Eat up.

79
00:05:28,036 --> 00:05:29,370
Oh, right.

80
00:05:29,454 --> 00:05:31,873
- You have it, Pa.
- He's diabetic too.

81
00:05:31,956 --> 00:05:34,709
We're limiting his consumption of meat.

82
00:05:36,794 --> 00:05:38,588
You can have it.

83
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:41,674
[CHUCKLES] Then I'll help myself.

84
00:05:41,758 --> 00:05:46,220
I love Auntie Precious's cooking.

85
00:05:46,304 --> 00:05:48,347
- It's delicious.
- Thank you.

86
00:05:48,431 --> 00:05:49,474
[CHUCKLES]

87
00:05:50,808 --> 00:05:53,895
I know adobo is your favorite.

88
00:05:53,978 --> 00:05:56,981
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

89
00:05:57,065 --> 00:05:58,441
You remember?

90
00:05:59,984 --> 00:06:03,196
It's Mama's specialty after all.

91
00:06:04,155 --> 00:06:05,031
[BEA CHUCKLES]

92
00:06:05,114 --> 00:06:06,991
Which tastes better?

93
00:06:07,075 --> 00:06:12,121
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

94
00:06:12,205 --> 00:06:13,331
Oliver.

95
00:06:14,457 --> 00:06:18,669
Any food will surely taste good

96
00:06:19,796 --> 00:06:22,965
if it was cooked with love.

97
00:06:24,217 --> 00:06:27,470
I'm sure Auntie Precious
cooked this with love.

98
00:06:27,553 --> 00:06:29,222
That's why it tastes good. [CHUCKLES]

99
00:06:30,765 --> 00:06:31,808
Eat up.

100
00:06:33,267 --> 00:06:36,437
By the way, Pa…

101
00:06:36,521 --> 00:06:38,940
I visited Mama.

102
00:06:39,023 --> 00:06:40,608
Oh, how is she doing?

103
00:06:41,651 --> 00:06:43,611
I feel sorry for her.

104
00:06:43,694 --> 00:06:45,988
She has bruises and scratches
all over her body.

105
00:06:47,740 --> 00:06:49,033
[ENRICO] What happened?

106
00:06:49,117 --> 00:06:51,744
They said she kept throwing a fit

107
00:06:51,828 --> 00:06:55,123
because she doesn't want to be alone.

108
00:06:55,206 --> 00:06:58,793
I told you, Pa. Mama can't be left alone.

109
00:07:00,711 --> 00:07:02,672
There are people there
who are looking after her.

110
00:07:02,755 --> 00:07:06,425
It's also safer for all of us
if she's there.

111
00:07:06,509 --> 00:07:12,890
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

112
00:07:16,310 --> 00:07:17,437
[ENRICO CLEARS THROAT]

113
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:20,815
This is really good.

114
00:07:22,108 --> 00:07:24,026
[BEA] It's so good. [CHUCKLES]

115
00:07:24,110 --> 00:07:29,407
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

116
00:07:29,490 --> 00:07:31,492
- Eat up.
- Mm-hmm.

117
00:07:32,994 --> 00:07:35,371
Mmm. So good.

118
00:07:39,208 --> 00:07:41,544
Uh, Billy?

119
00:07:42,170 --> 00:07:43,212
Thank you.

120
00:07:43,296 --> 00:07:46,382
Thank you for the lunch. I enjoyed it.

121
00:07:47,383 --> 00:07:48,801
And also,

122
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:52,763
I'm sorry for bringing up my mom earlier.

123
00:07:53,973 --> 00:07:56,976
I agree with you that it's better for her

124
00:07:58,269 --> 00:07:59,437
to stay at the hospital.

125
00:08:00,229 --> 00:08:03,107
But I hope you understand
that as a daughter,

126
00:08:03,191 --> 00:08:09,197
I just want to be sure that
my mother is doing okay.

127
00:08:10,364 --> 00:08:13,242
Things are finally looking better
for my family now.

128
00:08:14,494 --> 00:08:16,871
They almost died because of the fire.

129
00:08:16,954 --> 00:08:19,874
The fire that your mother started.

130
00:08:19,957 --> 00:08:22,043
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

131
00:08:22,126 --> 00:08:26,339
So you understand why
she can't be absolved, right?

132
00:08:28,925 --> 00:08:30,009
Now, about Caloy…

133
00:08:31,886 --> 00:08:34,555
Do you know he escaped?

134
00:08:39,727 --> 00:08:41,062
You didn't know?

135
00:08:42,104 --> 00:08:43,105
Huh?

136
00:08:44,190 --> 00:08:45,775
You're no longer in touch?

137
00:08:46,859 --> 00:08:48,569
N-N… No!

138
00:08:48,653 --> 00:08:52,031
[SCOFFS] Billy, how would we get in touch?

139
00:08:52,114 --> 00:08:54,784
I don't have his number.

140
00:08:54,867 --> 00:08:57,662
We're… We're not…
We're not together, remember?

141
00:08:57,745 --> 00:09:00,248
But I hope he does contact me.

142
00:09:01,249 --> 00:09:02,250
What?

143
00:09:03,459 --> 00:09:05,127
I hope he contacts me

144
00:09:05,211 --> 00:09:08,798
so I can then tell you,
and you can have him arrested.

145
00:09:08,881 --> 00:09:11,551
Billy, um…

146
00:09:11,634 --> 00:09:14,303
I know it's hard to believe,

147
00:09:14,387 --> 00:09:18,558
but I hope you know that I'm on your side.

148
00:09:18,641 --> 00:09:23,938
I will do everything I can
to help you catch that Caloy.

149
00:09:25,022 --> 00:09:26,274
I swear I'll do anything.

150
00:09:27,149 --> 00:09:30,069
Trust me, we're on the same side now.

151
00:09:30,152 --> 00:09:33,698
I mean, you've helped me so much.

152
00:09:34,949 --> 00:09:37,243
Billy, I'll help you.

153
00:09:37,326 --> 00:09:38,869
We'll send him to jail.

154
00:09:38,953 --> 00:09:39,996
That's a promise.

155
00:09:41,122 --> 00:09:42,331
- Okay?
- [OLIVER] Bea!

156
00:09:43,207 --> 00:09:45,376
Uh, Bea…

157
00:09:45,459 --> 00:09:48,212
We packed you some adobo to take home.

158
00:09:48,296 --> 00:09:50,965
- This is for me?
- Yes.

159
00:09:51,048 --> 00:09:53,301
Wow, this is my favorite.

160
00:09:53,384 --> 00:09:55,303
Thank you. Thank--

161
00:09:55,386 --> 00:09:57,805
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

162
00:09:57,888 --> 00:10:00,725
- Thank you, little bro.
- Okay.

163
00:10:00,808 --> 00:10:02,935
This is great.
I'll have some food for later.

164
00:10:03,019 --> 00:10:05,813
I'll go now, Billy. Thanks again.

165
00:10:06,397 --> 00:10:08,649
- Take care.
- Thank you.

166
00:10:17,325 --> 00:10:23,164
[MUSIC BECOMES GLOOMY]

167
00:10:23,247 --> 00:10:27,627
[LINE RINGING]

168
00:10:27,710 --> 00:10:33,382
[PHONE BUZZING]

169
00:10:33,466 --> 00:10:35,676
[BUSY TONE]

170
00:10:38,471 --> 00:10:39,889
[BUSY TONE]

171
00:10:45,519 --> 00:10:47,480
[LINE RINGING]

172
00:10:47,563 --> 00:10:50,399
[PHONE BUZZING]

173
00:10:52,234 --> 00:10:53,527
[BUSY TONE]

174
00:10:57,323 --> 00:10:59,784
[PHONE BUZZING]

175
00:11:05,373 --> 00:11:07,208
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

176
00:11:09,418 --> 00:11:10,753
We're still closed.

177
00:11:12,004 --> 00:11:13,255
Come back later.

178
00:11:14,799 --> 00:11:18,969
[DOOR CREAKS OPEN]

179
00:11:21,013 --> 00:11:22,181
Can we talk?

180
00:11:22,264 --> 00:11:26,644
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

181
00:11:38,781 --> 00:11:45,788
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

182
00:11:50,501 --> 00:11:51,585
You know,

183
00:11:53,212 --> 00:11:58,259
I heard Grandpa and Mom's
conversation back then.

184
00:12:00,386 --> 00:12:06,225
Grandpa was urging her to leave you.

185
00:12:07,017 --> 00:12:10,688
Because as well as physically hurting her,

186
00:12:11,605 --> 00:12:14,066
you also had the gall to cheat on her.

187
00:12:14,150 --> 00:12:18,571
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

188
00:12:18,654 --> 00:12:20,239
It's okay. Be honest with me.

189
00:12:20,322 --> 00:12:21,824
Who's your mistress?

190
00:12:22,992 --> 00:12:24,118
Karen?

191
00:12:25,494 --> 00:12:26,787
[CLEARS THROAT]

192
00:12:29,498 --> 00:12:31,834
You didn't respect Mom.

193
00:12:33,544 --> 00:12:36,714
You even gave her necklace
to your mistress.

194
00:12:39,216 --> 00:12:40,259
Unbelievable.

195
00:12:42,011 --> 00:12:43,554
Um…

196
00:12:43,637 --> 00:12:45,014
Jordan, uh…

197
00:12:47,516 --> 00:12:49,685
I can't change what happened in the past.

198
00:12:51,854 --> 00:12:53,481
I regret it all.

199
00:12:55,483 --> 00:12:57,359
But if…
[EXHALES SHARPLY]

200
00:12:57,443 --> 00:13:00,571
…you'll let me prove to you that

201
00:13:00,654 --> 00:13:02,114
I've changed,

202
00:13:02,198 --> 00:13:03,866
I want to make it up to you.

203
00:13:04,825 --> 00:13:08,954
If you'll give me a chance,
I'm going to change for the better.

204
00:13:10,456 --> 00:13:11,749
[DINO] <i>Here, Jordan.</i>

205
00:13:11,832 --> 00:13:13,417
<i>Thank you, Daddy!</i>

206
00:13:13,501 --> 00:13:14,793
<i>- Oh.</i>
- [YOUNG JORDAN CHUCKLES]

207
00:13:14,877 --> 00:13:17,213
<i>- Okay, go. Open it.</i>
- [YOUNG JORDAN CHUCKLES]

208
00:13:19,840 --> 00:13:21,425
<i>Okay.</i>

209
00:13:21,509 --> 00:13:24,220
<i>I got you a ukulele.</i>
<i>Just a small one for now.</i>

210
00:13:24,303 --> 00:13:27,139
<i>- So you can reach the…</i>
<i>- Wow!</i>

211
00:13:27,223 --> 00:13:29,934
<i>Once your hands get bigger,</i>
<i>I'll get you a real guitar.</i>

212
00:13:30,017 --> 00:13:32,061
<i>But the chords are the same.</i>

213
00:13:32,144 --> 00:13:35,105
<i>- Thank you!</i>
<i>- You're welcome, bud!</i>

214
00:13:36,315 --> 00:13:39,693
[UKULELE STRUMMING]

215
00:13:39,777 --> 00:13:41,153
<i>Thank you, Daddy!</i>

216
00:13:42,112 --> 00:13:43,739
[DINO] <i>You're welcome.</i>

217
00:13:45,449 --> 00:13:49,662
[JADE SINGING]
<i>♪ I'll ride your wave ♪</i>

218
00:13:49,745 --> 00:13:53,832
<i>♪ Wherever it takes me ♪</i>

219
00:13:53,916 --> 00:13:59,505
<i>♪ Do you know when I found you</i>
<i>Everything changed? ♪</i>

220
00:13:59,588 --> 00:14:02,341
<i>♪ Wherever I go ♪</i>

221
00:14:02,424 --> 00:14:06,512
[JADE, YOUNG JORDAN SINGING]
<i>♪ My heart won't be lost ♪</i>

222
00:14:06,595 --> 00:14:10,599
<i>♪ Even if you let go, I'll come back ♪</i>

223
00:14:10,683 --> 00:14:15,479
<i>♪ Do you know when I found you</i>
<i>Everything changed? ♪</i>

224
00:14:15,563 --> 00:14:17,398
<i>♪ Stay right there, my love ♪</i>

225
00:14:17,481 --> 00:14:21,235
<i>♪ Because I'm coming home ♪</i>

226
00:14:21,318 --> 00:14:22,820
[YOUNG JORDAN CHUCKLES]

227
00:14:24,071 --> 00:14:25,030
[SOFT CHUCKLE]

228
00:14:27,366 --> 00:14:28,826
How are you going to do that?

229
00:14:28,909 --> 00:14:30,160
Look at you.

230
00:14:30,953 --> 00:14:32,329
You're a fugitive.

231
00:14:33,622 --> 00:14:38,335
[CLEARS THROAT]
Um, aside from your forgiveness…

232
00:14:40,588 --> 00:14:43,257
of course, I also need money
to start again.

233
00:14:45,551 --> 00:14:47,428
Now, the truth comes out.

234
00:14:48,679 --> 00:14:50,723
All you want from me is money.

235
00:14:50,806 --> 00:14:52,057
That's why you came to me.

236
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:54,101
Dad.

237
00:14:55,519 --> 00:14:56,770
Just surrender to the authorities.

238
00:14:56,854 --> 00:14:59,106
Surrender? I can't do that.

239
00:14:59,899 --> 00:15:02,776
What if Caloy targets you again?
Who's going to protect you?

240
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:04,987
- I can protect myself.
- You can protect yourself?

241
00:15:05,070 --> 00:15:07,197
How many times
did Caloy put you in danger?

242
00:15:07,281 --> 00:15:09,491
Now it's me asking you for help.

243
00:15:09,575 --> 00:15:13,662
[SCOFFS] Okay. So saving me
comes with a price?

244
00:15:15,039 --> 00:15:16,665
Just so we're clear.

245
00:15:17,333 --> 00:15:18,959
Really clear.

246
00:15:19,043 --> 00:15:22,880
Dad, you won't get any money from me.

247
00:15:24,089 --> 00:15:24,924
Okay?

248
00:15:26,717 --> 00:15:27,843
You know,

249
00:15:28,552 --> 00:15:32,932
you're so stingy for someone
who earns so much.

250
00:15:33,015 --> 00:15:37,227
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

251
00:15:38,312 --> 00:15:41,190
I owe you nothing.

252
00:15:43,067 --> 00:15:44,777
My answer is no.

253
00:15:48,447 --> 00:15:50,115
Well, think again, hmm?

254
00:15:51,075 --> 00:15:53,786
That song that made you famous?

255
00:15:54,578 --> 00:15:56,330
Who do you think
your mother wrote that for?

256
00:15:56,413 --> 00:15:57,915
For you? No.

257
00:15:59,124 --> 00:16:01,377
She wrote it for the two of us.

258
00:16:05,130 --> 00:16:06,090
Yes.

259
00:16:07,925 --> 00:16:09,468
It was for you too.

260
00:16:11,845 --> 00:16:14,390
But that was before
you started hurting her.

261
00:16:14,473 --> 00:16:16,308
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

262
00:16:16,392 --> 00:16:20,229
No matter what you say,
I deserve my share.

263
00:16:21,897 --> 00:16:23,023
Get out.

264
00:16:23,899 --> 00:16:25,150
Excuse me?

265
00:16:25,234 --> 00:16:27,319
- Get out!
- No!

266
00:16:27,403 --> 00:16:29,029
- If you don't leave…
- What?

267
00:16:29,113 --> 00:16:30,239
I'm calling…

268
00:16:30,322 --> 00:16:31,573
Who? The cops?

269
00:16:31,657 --> 00:16:34,535
- Don't touch me! Get off me!
- You'll call the cops?

270
00:16:34,618 --> 00:16:35,995
- You bastard!
- [BLOW LANDS]

271
00:16:36,078 --> 00:16:37,913
[TENSE BEAT]

272
00:16:37,997 --> 00:16:38,998
[GRUNTS]

273
00:16:39,081 --> 00:16:44,420
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

274
00:16:51,301 --> 00:16:56,098
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

275
00:17:02,187 --> 00:17:03,397
[GRUNTS SOFTLY]

276
00:17:06,025 --> 00:17:07,067
[SIGHS]

277
00:17:07,151 --> 00:17:13,490
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

278
00:17:16,785 --> 00:17:18,787
- [INHALES, GRUNTS ANGRILY]
- [SLAMS FLOOR]

279
00:17:22,207 --> 00:17:28,630
[GRIM MUSIC CONTINUES]

280
00:17:36,930 --> 00:17:39,391
<i>Yes. We were in a relationship before,</i>

281
00:17:39,475 --> 00:17:41,518
<i>but that was a long time ago.</i>

282
00:17:41,602 --> 00:17:43,562
<i>We've been separated for a long time now.</i>

283
00:17:43,645 --> 00:17:45,564
[OFFICER] <i>Why didn't you</i>
<i>report him to us?</i>

284
00:17:46,356 --> 00:17:49,109
<i>I mean, I was scared.</i>

285
00:17:49,193 --> 00:17:51,487
<i>What if he hurt me? Right?</i>

286
00:17:51,570 --> 00:17:53,197
<i>Don't you get that?</i>

287
00:17:54,698 --> 00:17:56,075
<i>Dude, you were right.</i>

288
00:17:59,161 --> 00:18:01,580
<i>I was wrong to hope</i>

289
00:18:02,790 --> 00:18:04,291
<i>he would change.</i>

290
00:18:06,460 --> 00:18:07,878
<i>I didn't listen.</i>

291
00:18:10,047 --> 00:18:16,428
[SOBBING]

292
00:18:21,475 --> 00:18:23,060
[SOBS]

293
00:18:27,773 --> 00:18:29,650
<i>I only got my hopes up</i>

294
00:18:30,984 --> 00:18:33,028
<i>because I felt like…</i>

295
00:18:35,030 --> 00:18:36,907
<i>he was all I had left.</i>

296
00:18:39,201 --> 00:18:40,327
<i>Mom is dead.</i>

297
00:18:41,453 --> 00:18:43,247
<i>Grandpa Jude…</i>

298
00:18:43,330 --> 00:18:45,791
<i>He's still alive,</i>
<i>but it's like he's not even here.</i>

299
00:18:46,416 --> 00:18:48,043
<i>It's just hard to accept…</i>

300
00:18:49,795 --> 00:18:51,713
<i>that he's the only family I have left.</i>

301
00:18:52,381 --> 00:18:53,841
<i>And this is what happens.</i>

302
00:18:55,092 --> 00:18:58,720
<i>Why did I have to have</i>
<i>such a terrible father?</i>

303
00:19:01,390 --> 00:19:03,142
<i>But you're not like him.</i>

304
00:19:05,853 --> 00:19:06,770
<i>Right?</i>

305
00:19:07,604 --> 00:19:09,982
<i>You're nothing like your father.</i>

306
00:19:10,816 --> 00:19:13,569
<i>Because you are better than him.</i>

307
00:19:13,652 --> 00:19:17,865
["AAMININ" BY JAMES REID PLAYING]

308
00:19:17,948 --> 00:19:19,908
<i>There is nothing wrong</i>

309
00:19:19,992 --> 00:19:24,329
<i>with hoping the people we love</i>
<i>will love us back.</i>

310
00:19:25,789 --> 00:19:26,707
<i>But…</i>

311
00:19:30,043 --> 00:19:33,547
<i>when you're getting hurt</i>
<i>over and over again,</i>

312
00:19:34,506 --> 00:19:37,259
<i>I have to draw the line.</i>

313
00:19:38,719 --> 00:19:41,096
<i>I won't let you do this anymore, okay?</i>

314
00:19:48,437 --> 00:19:54,526
["AAMININ" CONTINUES]

315
00:20:10,876 --> 00:20:17,299
["AAMININ" CONTINUES]

316
00:20:25,098 --> 00:20:31,146
["AAMININ" CONTINUES]
